// APSS One RFQ explanatory notes. Proposal only; not implementation or compliance certification.
return [["7.1 / 7.11",["A prospect submits an application online, selects a membership level and sees exactly which information and evidence is required.","APSS staff review the application, request missing documents, approve or decline and notify the applicant automatically.","Members see expiry dates, renewal payments, receipts, buddy onboarding and their seven-stage growth journey.","APSS can configure new membership levels and benefits without hiring a developer."],["Explain joining rules and missing steps; draft renewal notices for staff approval; flag members stalled six months. Eligibility and approvals remain rule-based and human-controlled."]],["7.2",["Each eligible Professional Member maintains a biography, profile photo, speaking topics, industries, languages, showreel and downloadable materials.","Corporate visitors filter by subject and expertise and send an enquiry to the speaker or APSS.","Public visibility follows active membership, permissions and approved profile settings; a lapsed speaker is hidden automatically.","Private contact details and administrative notes never appear in the public directory."],["Match an event brief to speakers using only approved public profile details; explain why each match fits; let visitors refine their search."]],["7.3",["APSS creates member-only SIGs, Kampong groups and mentor/mastermind spaces with named group leaders.","Members post questions, share permitted files, comment and receive searchable announcements and digest emails.","Leaders moderate contributions and permission rules remove access when membership lapses.","Important announcements stay easy to locate instead of disappearing in a busy chat thread."],["Summarise approved discussions, recommend related resources and draft weekly digests for moderators; never reveal private group content to outsiders."]],["7.4",["An authorised organiser chooses an event template and enters date, format, venue/Zoom link, speakers, capacity and attendance rules.","The system offers free RSVP or member/guest/early-bird prices, registration confirmations, waiting lists and reminders.","On arrival, volunteers check in attendees; attendance flows into member journey and event eligibility records.","Special formats can add speaker applications, coach panels, volunteers and judges as required."],["Draft event descriptions and reminder messages; suggest schedules and related programmes; summarise post-event feedback. AI does not fabricate registrations, check-in or payment results."]],["7.5",["Convention organisers publish a branded public programme and manage multi-day passes and session selections.","Buyers can receive tickets and invoices, while staff manage speakers, sponsors, volunteers, capacity and check-in.","Awards support nominations and reviews; speaking competitions support rounds and phone-based judges' scores.","Convention planning stays connected to APSS's existing internal application through agreed count/ticket exports, rather than automatically replacing it."],["Draft speaker calls, participant FAQs, programme summaries and attendee communications, always reviewed before release."]],["7.6 / Appendix B",["Members browse four assessed Core Modules and 26 electives across Expertise, Eloquence, Enterprise and Ethics.","Each course shows prerequisites, dates, fees, protected resources, enrolment, attendance and course progress.","Assessors receive only assigned work; rubrics, conflict checks, written feedback, second reviews, resits and appeals are recorded.","Members and administrators see completion evidence, certificates and progress toward Professional membership."],["Suggest appropriate electives and create feedback drafts from approved rubrics; a qualified human assessor makes the formal decision."]],["7.6 / 7.11",["Members see CPD points and the supporting learning evidence for each period.","Mentors accept requests, log sessions and record cycle reports with appropriate privacy controls.","The system calculates eligibility indicators for AM-to-PM progression, CSP review and certificates against APSS rules.","Administrators handle exceptions and maintain a permanent decision history."],["Suggest a next learning step or mentor match; identify missing evidence; summarise activity without issuing qualifications automatically."]],["7.7 / Appendix D",["Admins build a targeted list from live member data rather than copied spreadsheets.","Templates send approved onboarding, expiry, payment, registration and post-event messages.","Consent, unsubscribes, suppression rules, delivery reports and staff approval are recorded.","Members can choose relevant notification preferences."],["Draft clearer messages, translate or adapt tone, propose audience segments and summarise campaign results; sends require permission and approval."]],["7.8 / 10",["A single checkout will cover memberships, annual renewals, classes, events and Convention passes while retaining one member/customer record.","Stripe is the proposed primary gateway for credit/debit cards and PayNow in SGD for eligible Singapore accounts. PayPal may be offered as an optional international checkout method. APSS will own the gateway accounts.","Following confirmed transactions, the system records registration or membership payment status and issues receipts. A proposed Xero Cloud connector maps invoices, contacts, payments and refunds, prevents duplicates, retries failures and logs discrepancies.","Finance staff can manage discounts, refund requests, payment exceptions, reconciliation and exports using access permissions and audit logs. Gateway processing fees, Xero subscriptions and provider charges are paid by APSS and excluded from the fixed development fee."],["Identify unmatched transactions and draft finance summaries; accounting postings and refunds stay deterministic and subject to approval."]],["7.9 / 11",["A refreshed public website includes an editable directory, programmes, events, editorial content and contact routes.","APSS volunteers can change ordinary pages and images without developer involvement.","The design works on phones and tablets and preserves search visibility through redirects, metadata and accessible templates.","The website shares an identity and data flow with the member platform rather than duplicating member records."],["Help staff draft articles, descriptions and metadata from approved sources; humans review content before publication."]],["7.10 / 8",["Portfolio directors see only the tasks, members and information necessary for their responsibilities.","The ExCo console provides approvals, nominations, committee handover workflows, audit trails and policy links.","Staff can configure role assignments and transfer responsibilities as elected terms change.","Sensitive activities use MFA, retention policies and reviewable approval history."],["Summarise permitted meeting records, draft action lists, explain policies and surface outstanding approvals; no unapproved autonomous governance decisions."]],["7.11 / 8 / 9",["ExCo dashboards track join/renewal trends, member growth stages, attendance, PD progress and revenue.","Reports can be filtered and exported, with different views for membership, event, learning and finance teams.","Data must be migrated from existing tools with duplicate reconciliation and documented acceptance tests.","Scale, backup/restore, permissions and PDPA controls support long-term operation."],["Let authorised staff ask questions about approved reports and receive traceable summaries; source permissions and data quality checks remain enforced."]]];
